1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,140
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:03,510
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:05,180
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:08,310
(Episode 14)

5
00:00:08,650 --> 00:00:12,080
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

6
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:36,230
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

7
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:13,070
(Hospital Room)

8
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:16,940
Hello.

9
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,280
Where are you?

10
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:21,050
- At the hospital.
- Are you with Ko Eun Seol?

11
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:24,780
Chairman Kim asked me
to look after her.

12
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:26,480
Doesn't she have any family?

13
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:27,820
Why are you the one
looking after her?

14
00:02:27,890 --> 00:02:28,890
Get back here already.

15
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:30,760
Hae Ra.

16
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:32,820
Get over here, darn it!

17
00:02:33,830 --> 00:02:36,760
All right, just stop yelling.
I'll be there soon.

18
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:41,730
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

19
00:02:55,850 --> 00:02:56,920
Did I wake you?

20
00:02:58,280 --> 00:02:59,280
Was that Hae Ra?

21
00:03:01,950 --> 00:03:02,950
Yes.

22
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:06,360
Aren't you going
to call your family?

23
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:08,530
There's no need to worry them.

24
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:11,230
I'll be fine by myself,
so you can go.

25
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:13,130
Still, I can't just leave you.

26
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:14,730
Really, I'm fine.

27
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,840
(Hospital Room, VIP 1,
Patient Name: Ko Eun Seol)

28
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:23,640
Eun Seol, are you okay?

29
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:27,050
Attorney Seo, you didn't have
to come all this way.

30
00:03:27,050 --> 00:03:28,410
I'm not even that hurt.

31
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:29,980
What do you mean
you're not that hurt?

32
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:31,680
I heard you got ten stitches.

33
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:33,050
Mr. Seo, how are you here?

34
00:03:35,450 --> 00:03:36,690
Chief Cha.

35
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,290
Do you two know each other?

36
00:03:42,460 --> 00:03:43,460
Yes.

37
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:45,260
How?

38
00:03:46,430 --> 00:03:47,500
We're just acquaintances.

39
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:51,270
Now that Attorney Seo is here,
you can go, Seok Jin.

40
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:54,010
Yes, I'll stay with her.

41
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:56,140
You can go now, Chief Cha.

42
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:01,610
Well, all right.

43
00:04:02,710 --> 00:04:03,850
Get some rest and recover well.

44
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:06,420
Thank you so much for today.

45
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,360
There you are.

46
00:04:14,130 --> 00:04:15,130
What was that all about earlier?

47
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:17,460
What do you mean?

48
00:04:18,230 --> 00:04:20,800
Why were you carrying Ko Eun Seol
in your arms and running?

49
00:04:21,470 --> 00:04:23,800
What was I supposed to do?
Leave an injured person there?

50
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,070
You could've called 911.

51
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:27,540
Why did you carry her
instead of calling 911?

52
00:04:28,970 --> 00:04:31,040
She's the one who got hurt
saving your mother.

53
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:32,610
Aren't you grateful at all?

54
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:35,650
- That's beside the point.
- Kang Hae Ra.

55
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:39,020
If it weren't for Ko Eun Seol,

56
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:41,250
your mother could've been
seriously hurt.

57
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:44,160
Shouldn't you ask
how she's doing first?

58
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:46,360
I'm really disappointed.

59
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:49,390
You're disappointed?

60
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:53,900
I know why you're angry,
but this isn't right.

61
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,040
You don't care how I feel, do you?

62
00:04:58,070 --> 00:04:59,570
Do you have any idea
how I felt earlier?

63
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:02,410
It made my blood boil. But what?

64
00:05:02,910 --> 00:05:04,640
You're disappointed
that I didn't ask about her?

65
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:07,050
I'm the one who's disappointed.

66
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:09,580
I'm the one
who's disappointed in you.

67
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:24,430
Unbelievable.

68
00:05:36,310 --> 00:05:38,810
It's hot. Gosh, it's so hot.

69
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:41,410
What kind of house
doesn't have air conditioning?

70
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:42,850
How are people supposed to live?

71
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:46,150
- It's so hot.
- Man, it's hot.

72
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:47,990
- Mom.
- It's hot, isn't it?

73
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:49,050
Just bear with it for this year.

74
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:51,260
I'll get us an AC unit
next year, okay?

75
00:05:51,490 --> 00:05:54,760
I don't know
if I'll even be alive next year.

76
00:05:58,230 --> 00:05:59,230
Forget it.

77
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:00,230
- Dad.
- Yes?

78
00:06:00,230 --> 00:06:04,470
- Eun Seol got hurt.
- How? Where? How badly?

79
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:06,370
Let's just go.
I'll tell you on the way.

80
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:09,140
Okay, let's go together.
Mom, I'll be back.

81
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:13,310
Now what's all this about?

82
00:06:13,850 --> 00:06:16,380
Gosh, it's so hot.

83
00:06:17,350 --> 00:06:18,480
I can't take this anymore.

84
00:06:22,950 --> 00:06:24,720
Is anyone home?

85
00:06:28,490 --> 00:06:29,630
Oh, it's so cool.

86
00:06:30,930 --> 00:06:32,300
This is paradise.

87
00:06:33,870 --> 00:06:34,870
Oh, my.

88
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:37,670
Why are you in our house?

89
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:40,200
Wait, are you here alone?

90
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:41,340
Yes.

91
00:06:41,470 --> 00:06:43,440
- Where's your mom?
- She went to the market.

92
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:44,980
Oh, really?

93
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:48,110
It's so nice and cool. Oh, my.

94
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:50,480
What were you doing by yourself?

95
00:06:50,650 --> 00:06:52,280
I was reading a picture book.

96
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:54,850
Then how about you read it to me?

97
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:56,890
- Sure.
- You're so sweet.

98
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,760
"The Jjayo Jjayo Fairy
eats anything."

99
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:07,530
"It eats crunchy autumn leaves,
munches on roses,"

100
00:07:07,630 --> 00:07:10,300
"and slurps up the red sunset."

101
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:16,170
"When the full moon rises,
it flutters down on a moonbeam."

102
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:20,410
"The Jjayo Jjayo Fairy
comes down from the moon."

103
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:26,080
"From the moon,
the Jjayo Jjayo Fairy..."

104
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:38,300
What the...

105
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:40,030
What's going on?

106
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:44,300
Teun Teun.

107
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:46,400
Teun Teun?

108
00:07:47,510 --> 00:07:49,470
- Mom, you're back.
- Hey.

109
00:07:50,370 --> 00:07:52,940
What is this lady doing here?

110
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:56,180
I don't know. She asked me
to read her a book, so I did.

111
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:58,250
She started snoring
and fell asleep right away.

112
00:07:58,550 --> 00:08:01,020
It got so loud, I went into my room.

113
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:06,560
Ma'am.

114
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:09,930
Ma'am, please wake up. Ma'am.

115
00:08:09,930 --> 00:08:10,960
What?

116
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,570
You're back.

117
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,900
What are you doing here?

118
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:21,170
The annex is ridiculously hot.

119
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:26,310
How can you rent out
a place like that?

120
00:08:27,350 --> 00:08:28,610
If you don't like it that much,

121
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:31,780
I can give you back your deposit,
and you can move out.

122
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:34,820
How am I supposed to move again
in this heat wave?

123
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:36,150
I'll just have to put up with it.

124
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:38,390
Please leave now.

125
00:08:39,690 --> 00:08:42,930
Come on.
Can't I stay a little longer?

126
00:08:43,730 --> 00:08:46,600
It isn't like my presence
will drive up your power bill.

127
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:51,800
I'm sorry.

128
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:55,070
Last month's electricity bill
was too high.

129
00:08:56,310 --> 00:08:59,080
A mother this heartless?

130
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:01,550
What kind of example is she setting
for her child?

131
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,450
Oh, my knees.

132
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:07,990
What a sweet nap that was.

133
00:09:16,030 --> 00:09:17,060
What happened?

134
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,060
Are you hurt badly?

135
00:09:19,330 --> 00:09:20,330
You came.

136
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:23,600
Did you contact them, Attorney Seo?

137
00:09:24,170 --> 00:09:25,170
Yes.

138
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:28,470
I heard you were stabbed.
Where's that punk?

139
00:09:29,370 --> 00:09:31,510
I'm okay. I'm not hurt badly.

140
00:09:31,580 --> 00:09:33,310
Where the heck is that punk?

141
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:34,910
He's in police custody.

142
00:09:35,510 --> 00:09:36,610
Which police station?

143
00:09:37,650 --> 00:09:40,280
Why are you asking?
Are you going to beat him up too?

144
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:42,320
Should I just let him
get away with it?

145
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:44,120
He stabbed my sister.

146
00:09:44,890 --> 00:09:46,390
I understand how you feel, Eun Guk.

147
00:09:46,990 --> 00:09:48,290
But you won't be able to see him
even if you go.

148
00:09:50,290 --> 00:09:51,300
Eun Guk.

149
00:09:53,930 --> 00:09:54,930
So?

150
00:09:55,630 --> 00:09:57,340
Where are you hurt, and how badly?

151
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:01,210
I'm fine. It's nothing serious.

152
00:10:03,010 --> 00:10:05,280
What if this leaves a scar?

153
00:10:29,130 --> 00:10:31,640
(Ko Eun Seol)

154
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:34,440
(No search results found)

155
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:51,890
Ma'am, what would you like
for lunch?

156
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,330
Are you going somewhere?

157
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:59,330
I'm going to visit the young woman
before she's discharged.

158
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,230
You can't.

159
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:03,370
You're in no condition
to go out yet.

160
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,400
I'm fine.

161
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:10,810
Please, just stay home.
Or I can go in your place.

162
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:15,450
How can I, when she's the one
who saved my life?

163
00:11:17,310 --> 00:11:18,720
I have to go.

164
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:21,290
Then I'll go with you.

165
00:11:29,890 --> 00:11:30,900
Yes?

166
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:44,040
Madam Chairman.

167
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:47,210
It isn't much, but here you go.

168
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,610
Are you feeling better?

169
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,920
Yes, I'm being discharged tomorrow.

170
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:55,820
Thank goodness it wasn't any worse.

171
00:11:56,990 --> 00:12:00,390
I heard you and Hae Ra went
to high school together.

172
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:01,530
Your name...

173
00:12:01,730 --> 00:12:02,930
It's Ko Eun Seol.

174
00:12:02,990 --> 00:12:05,660
Eun Seol, thank you so much.

175
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:09,600
If it hadn't been for you,
I would've been in real trouble.

176
00:12:10,070 --> 00:12:12,200
I'm so glad you're safe.

177
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:13,900
That being said,

178
00:12:14,270 --> 00:12:17,010
I'd like to offer you
financial compensation.

179
00:12:17,410 --> 00:12:19,080
No, that's all right.

180
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,680
Please.

181
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,580
Please accept
this token of appreciation.

182
00:12:22,650 --> 00:12:24,850
It'd really put my mind at ease.

183
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:29,890
No. I really don't need
any financial compensation, ma'am.

184
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:32,090
Then other than money,

185
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,830
is there anything else you want?

186
00:12:38,830 --> 00:12:39,900
Tell me.

187
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:42,430
If it's within my power,
I'll grant it.

188
00:12:43,270 --> 00:12:45,770
Are you sure
you don't mind me saying it?

189
00:12:46,070 --> 00:12:47,270
Not at all.

190
00:12:47,710 --> 00:12:48,710
What is it?

191
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:50,880
Well...

192
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,280
I'd like a job at Cheongma.

193
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:57,110
You want to join our company?

194
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:58,180
Yes.

195
00:12:58,250 --> 00:12:59,780
That's out of the question, Ms. Ko.

196
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:01,320
Why not?

197
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:03,720
I can just hire her
through special recruitment.

198
00:13:03,790 --> 00:13:06,790
Ms. Ko was already eliminated
from the competition.

199
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:08,990
We can't overturn the results
for personal reasons...

200
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:10,860
and hire her
through special recruitment.

201
00:13:11,430 --> 00:13:13,560
The one who overturned the results
based on personal feelings...

202
00:13:13,630 --> 00:13:15,230
was Team Leader Kang
in the first place.

203
00:13:16,370 --> 00:13:17,400
That was...

204
00:13:17,470 --> 00:13:19,800
well within Ms. Kang's authority.

205
00:13:21,210 --> 00:13:23,310
Hae Ra has authority,

206
00:13:23,370 --> 00:13:25,780
but as Chairman, I don't?

207
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:27,510
Ma'am.

208
00:13:29,710 --> 00:13:32,880
All right.
I'll discuss it with the CEO.

209
00:13:33,580 --> 00:13:35,390
Thank you, ma'am.

210
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:40,690
No way, Mom.

211
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:43,560
Stay out of this.

212
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:45,830
She wouldn't have had to ask
if it weren't for you.

213
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,530
But Mom...

214
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,030
She saved my life, honey.

215
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:52,340
Surely we can grant
a request like that.

216
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:53,900
It's not as if she lacks the skills.

217
00:13:55,670 --> 00:13:57,240
Director Joo,
what are your thoughts?

218
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:01,410
I completely understand
how the Chairman feels,

219
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:03,510
but the third task ended today,

220
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:06,020
and we're just waiting
on the final results now.

221
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:08,020
If we were to hire Ko Eun Seol
through special recruitment,

222
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:10,850
it could cause chaos both inside
and outside the company.

223
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:12,020
That's right.

224
00:14:12,090 --> 00:14:13,620
If we hire her
through a special track,

225
00:14:13,690 --> 00:14:15,860
what about
the remaining ten finalists?

226
00:14:16,090 --> 00:14:17,800
Don't you think
they'll complain about it?

227
00:14:19,430 --> 00:14:20,460
Honey,

228
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:23,000
do you still want to hire her
knowing the risks?

229
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,270
That's right.

230
00:14:27,370 --> 00:14:29,040
Just make do
with financial compensation.

231
00:14:29,810 --> 00:14:32,480
He's right, Mom. No one hates money.

232
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:35,010
She obviously just refused once
out of pride,

233
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,780
so give her some cash
and get it over with.

234
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:38,750
No.

235
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:41,750
That young woman didn't want money.

236
00:14:42,850 --> 00:14:44,990
Then what do you want to do?

237
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,530
I'm going to at least
give her a chance.

238
00:14:49,030 --> 00:14:50,360
What kind of chance?

239
00:14:51,230 --> 00:14:54,000
A chance to compete
in the final evaluation.

240
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:55,600
Mom!

241
00:14:56,530 --> 00:14:58,740
I'll tell her to compete as soon as
she's discharged from the hospital,

242
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:01,110
so include her in the evaluation.

243
00:15:01,510 --> 00:15:03,140
You can do that much, can't you?

244
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:08,810
Since she saved your life,
I suppose it's the least we can do.

245
00:15:09,250 --> 00:15:10,950
- Dad!
- But...

246
00:15:12,050 --> 00:15:15,990
you can't complain
even if she doesn't finish first.

247
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:18,290
Then give me your word, too.

248
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:20,420
I want Hae Ra removed as a judge.

249
00:15:21,390 --> 00:15:22,390
Mom,

250
00:15:22,590 --> 00:15:24,900
a stranger would think Ko Eun Seol
is your daughter, not me.

251
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:27,870
Hae Ra.
You shouldn't say things like that.

252
00:15:28,430 --> 00:15:30,900
I'm worried you'll mess
with the scores again.

253
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,870
Don't worry. I won't this time.

254
00:15:49,950 --> 00:15:52,490
Just don't be so obvious this time.

255
00:15:52,890 --> 00:15:54,860
What if Ko Eun Seol
gets first place?

256
00:15:55,260 --> 00:15:56,390
If it weren't for me
in the second round,

257
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:57,830
she would've taken 1st or 2nd place.

258
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:00,260
Just make sure
she doesn't get first place.

259
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:02,730
Second place won't get her the job.

260
00:16:03,730 --> 00:16:04,770
All right.

261
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:16,280
Yes, Chairman Kim.

262
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,080
Yes.

263
00:16:19,550 --> 00:16:20,550
Of course not.

264
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:22,890
I'm just grateful
you're giving me a chance.

265
00:16:23,850 --> 00:16:24,860
Sure.

266
00:16:25,290 --> 00:16:26,290
Got it.

267
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:30,160
Who was that?

268
00:16:30,590 --> 00:16:32,930
The Chairman.
She's giving me a chance to compete.

269
00:16:33,730 --> 00:16:37,230
You saved her life, and all you get
is a chance to compete, not a job?

270
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:39,340
Still, that's better than nothing.

271
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:41,240
Am I good to be discharged?

272
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:42,540
Yes.

273
00:16:42,610 --> 00:16:45,180
Then, can you drop me off
at Cheongma?

274
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:46,340
Aren't you going home?

275
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:48,310
I need to know
what the third task is.

276
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:50,080
All right.

277
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:53,620
For your third task,

278
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:56,350
you'll choose a product here
to redesign,

279
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:58,320
then handle both
the planning and marketing.

280
00:16:58,560 --> 00:16:59,790
When is it due?

281
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:00,890
By tomorrow morning.

282
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,490
That soon?

283
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:04,560
Hey.

284
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:06,260
Since you got this chance
through contacts,

285
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:08,000
you should at least handle
this much.

286
00:17:08,530 --> 00:17:10,330
What's wrong? Can't you do it?

287
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:12,400
Then just give up.

288
00:17:15,610 --> 00:17:16,740
Want to give up?

289
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:18,880
No.

290
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:20,780
After fighting for this opportunity?

291
00:17:21,910 --> 00:17:22,910
I'll do it.

292
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:25,180
Suit yourself.

293
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:45,770
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

294
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:48,340
Competing in the competition
with an injured leg?

295
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:54,980
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

296
00:17:55,050 --> 00:17:56,150
Hey, Mom.

297
00:17:57,310 --> 00:17:58,320
Dinner?

298
00:17:59,350 --> 00:18:01,750
Okay. I'll be right there. Sure.

299
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:35,350
Hey, Attorney Seo.

300
00:18:35,450 --> 00:18:38,420
Sorry. I didn't mean to startle you.

301
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:41,090
I didn't know you could do this.

302
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:42,560
I told you.

303
00:18:42,630 --> 00:18:44,760
I got every certification I could
while I was in there.

304
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
I thought you would've
gone home by now.

305
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:49,870
I was on my way out.

306
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:53,440
By the way, have you had dinner?

307
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:54,940
I don't have time for that.

308
00:18:56,110 --> 00:18:59,510
I figured as much,
so I brought you some gimbap.

309
00:19:00,610 --> 00:19:02,080
Here. Have this while you work.

310
00:19:04,550 --> 00:19:05,880
Go on.

311
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:11,560
Right, thanks for this.

312
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,670
Do you think you can finish it
by tomorrow morning?

313
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:28,210
I have to get it done somehow.

314
00:19:30,610 --> 00:19:32,780
I've met a lot of people in my life,

315
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:35,110
but none as determined as you.

316
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:45,860
Well, I'll get out of your hair.
You should get back to it.

317
00:19:46,690 --> 00:19:49,390
Right.
Thanks for the gimbap, Attorney Seo.

318
00:19:49,630 --> 00:19:52,500
Make sure you eat it all.
It's from a really good place.

319
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:59,340
Mom, I'm home.

320
00:20:01,670 --> 00:20:02,970
What's all this?

321
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,310
Hey, Seok Jin.

322
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:09,480
What are you doing here?

323
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:13,380
I came to have dinner
with you and your mom.

324
00:20:15,650 --> 00:20:16,790
You're home.

325
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,960
You must be hungry.
Go wash up real quick.

326
00:20:22,890 --> 00:20:23,890
Sure.

327
00:20:26,730 --> 00:20:27,730
Ms. Park.

328
00:20:29,070 --> 00:20:32,140
Try this. It's really expensive.

329
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:36,040
Oh, honestly. I can get it myself.

330
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:39,710
You have some too.

331
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:41,980
Sure.

332
00:20:43,750 --> 00:20:46,450
Really, what brings you here?
You didn't say you were coming.

333
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:51,460
I went too far the other day.

334
00:20:52,790 --> 00:20:54,760
Did you two fight?

335
00:20:55,530 --> 00:20:58,160
Yes, he hurt my feelings.

336
00:20:58,260 --> 00:21:00,200
Then why are you
the one apologizing?

337
00:21:00,530 --> 00:21:01,870
Tell me about it.

338
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:05,140
You must've been in the wrong.

339
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:06,140
No.

340
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:08,970
It's because I love him more.

341
00:21:09,510 --> 00:21:11,710
The one who loves more
is always at a disadvantage.

342
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:14,650
Right. Then...

343
00:21:14,710 --> 00:21:17,150
I suppose
you can stop liking Seok Jin.

344
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,490
Come on.

345
00:21:22,290 --> 00:21:23,290
Well...

346
00:21:26,090 --> 00:21:27,960
Anyway, I apologized.

347
00:21:30,730 --> 00:21:32,230
I got it, so eat up.

348
00:21:47,810 --> 00:21:49,050
All done.

349
00:21:57,450 --> 00:21:58,860
You may begin when you're ready.

350
00:21:59,020 --> 00:22:00,020
Right.

351
00:22:00,090 --> 00:22:01,830
(2026 Cheongma's Open Competition
for New Designers)

352
00:22:01,890 --> 00:22:03,930
I have a deep appreciation
for Cheongma's history.

353
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:06,860
(Key Features
of Cheongma's Signature Line)

354
00:22:06,930 --> 00:22:09,770
Cheongma was established to create
universal value for everyone.

355
00:22:09,830 --> 00:22:12,670
As a result,
it launched its signature line,

356
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:14,840
which became the solid foundation
of the company.

357
00:22:15,210 --> 00:22:17,770
My vision is
to modernize this heritage.

358
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:19,480
By doing so,
I will once again share...

359
00:22:19,540 --> 00:22:20,940
the founding spirit of Cheongma
with the world.

360
00:22:28,850 --> 00:22:31,290
Why are you the one
getting all nervous?

361
00:22:32,590 --> 00:22:33,720
My gosh.

362
00:22:33,990 --> 00:22:36,660
I don't know
why I'm acting like this.

363
00:22:36,890 --> 00:22:38,500
Don't get too invested.

364
00:22:38,730 --> 00:22:40,230
She didn't have much time,

365
00:22:40,360 --> 00:22:42,570
so it's unlikely to turn out
the way you want.

366
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:56,880
While the original product
might've seemed old and outdated,

367
00:22:56,950 --> 00:23:01,220
this new line will become
the new standard for a classic.

368
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:03,920
It won't just be targeted
at a specific age group.

369
00:23:03,990 --> 00:23:05,420
It'll appeal to every generation,

370
00:23:05,460 --> 00:23:07,690
from people in their 20s
to their 80s.

371
00:23:09,090 --> 00:23:10,430
I get what you're going for,

372
00:23:11,260 --> 00:23:14,330
but do you really think
that'll appeal to a younger crowd?

373
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:16,230
Last winter,

374
00:23:16,230 --> 00:23:18,600
chunky grandma-style vests
sold out everywhere,

375
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:22,170
becoming a huge fashion trend
among young people.

376
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:24,910
Similarly, if we combine...

377
00:23:24,980 --> 00:23:27,740
Cheongma's signature functionality
with a trendy touch,

378
00:23:27,910 --> 00:23:30,750
it'll become
the ultimate practical retro look...

379
00:23:30,810 --> 00:23:32,680
for young adults.

380
00:23:39,790 --> 00:23:42,530
Ko Eun Seol's evaluation
is over, Ms. Joo.

381
00:23:43,330 --> 00:23:45,700
So? Are the results in?

382
00:23:46,130 --> 00:23:47,130
Yes.

383
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:49,170
How did she do?

384
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:52,870
Come in.

385
00:23:56,870 --> 00:24:00,410
Sir, we've selected the winner
of the Design Competition.

386
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:02,210
Oh, really? Send them in.

387
00:24:03,010 --> 00:24:04,010
Please come in.

388
00:24:08,650 --> 00:24:09,820
Eun Seol!

389
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:17,360
Hello. I'm Ko Eun Seol.

390
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:19,760
So you seized your last chance
after all.

391
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:21,700
Congratulations.

392
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:24,900
Thank you, sir.

393
00:24:35,510 --> 00:24:40,120
Eun Seol, you got the job
and won prize money on top of that?

394
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:45,160
That's right. The prize money
is 50,000 dollars.

395
00:24:45,220 --> 00:24:46,220
What?

396
00:24:47,890 --> 00:24:51,460
So what are you going to do
with all that money?

397
00:24:51,900 --> 00:24:53,430
Don't get any ideas, Grandma.

398
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,500
She worked her fingers to the bone
to earn that money.

399
00:24:56,930 --> 00:24:59,070
Is she all you ever care about?

400
00:24:59,270 --> 00:25:01,570
You don't care about
my hard work at all.

401
00:25:03,870 --> 00:25:05,340
Do you need something, Grandma?

402
00:25:06,540 --> 00:25:10,550
Can't you just give me cash?
I'll spend it how I want.

403
00:25:11,210 --> 00:25:12,880
Mom, please.

404
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:15,050
How much do you need?

405
00:25:15,350 --> 00:25:16,350
How much?

406
00:25:17,350 --> 00:25:18,620
How much are you offering?

407
00:25:18,690 --> 00:25:19,860
Grandma, please.

408
00:25:20,190 --> 00:25:21,320
All right, fine.

409
00:25:22,930 --> 00:25:25,330
Anyway, you're definitely talented.

410
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:29,500
Pulling that off after doing
ten years of hard time...

411
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:31,700
- Mom!
- Grandma.

412
00:25:32,970 --> 00:25:36,170
What? Did I say something untrue?

413
00:25:40,780 --> 00:25:42,280
For crying out loud...

414
00:25:42,280 --> 00:25:44,750
Unbelievable.
What on earth happened?

415
00:25:44,850 --> 00:25:45,920
What do you mean?

416
00:25:46,520 --> 00:25:48,720
The judges' average score
placed her third.

417
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:51,660
How did Ko Eun Seol end up winning?

418
00:25:51,820 --> 00:25:53,860
Because they threw out
the highest and lowest scores.

419
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:55,790
What?

420
00:25:56,090 --> 00:25:59,230
So the score I gave her
didn't count.

421
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,260
Whose idea was that?

422
00:26:01,330 --> 00:26:02,470
The head judge.

423
00:26:02,770 --> 00:26:04,570
Something about fixing the problems
from the second round...

424
00:26:04,630 --> 00:26:06,540
Unbelievable.

425
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:08,640
My gosh.

426
00:26:09,540 --> 00:26:11,510
I didn't think of that.

427
00:26:12,710 --> 00:26:13,810
What do I do now?

428
00:26:13,940 --> 00:26:15,550
Isn't there a way
to stop Ko Eun Seol?

429
00:26:16,580 --> 00:26:18,920
What can we do
since she got in on talent?

430
00:26:19,220 --> 00:26:20,280
We'll just have to accept it.

431
00:26:21,050 --> 00:26:22,520
No, I refuse!

432
00:26:22,590 --> 00:26:24,820
I'd rather die
than work with Ko Eun Seol.

433
00:26:25,420 --> 00:26:27,420
Getting worked up
won't solve anything.

434
00:26:27,890 --> 00:26:30,130
Calm down and be rational.

435
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:34,100
Seriously!

436
00:26:39,840 --> 00:26:41,100
It's me, Professor Kim.

437
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:44,410
Thank you so much
for accepting my suggestion.

438
00:26:44,980 --> 00:26:45,980
Not at all.

439
00:26:46,510 --> 00:26:49,010
We couldn't repeat the same mistake
as the second round.

440
00:26:49,950 --> 00:26:52,580
In the end,
a talented candidate was chosen,

441
00:26:52,880 --> 00:26:54,020
so I'm very hopeful too.

442
00:26:55,020 --> 00:26:56,450
Same here.

443
00:26:57,720 --> 00:26:59,790
Yes, let's see each other soon.

444
00:27:18,210 --> 00:27:19,210
Congratulations.

445
00:27:20,110 --> 00:27:21,110
You did great.

446
00:27:22,050 --> 00:27:23,050
Thanks, Eun Guk.

447
00:27:25,420 --> 00:27:27,180
I hope your leg heals fast.

448
00:27:28,220 --> 00:27:29,220
I'm worried about it.

449
00:27:29,820 --> 00:27:30,890
It's almost all better.

450
00:27:33,190 --> 00:27:35,730
By the way,
is there anything you want to do?

451
00:27:36,560 --> 00:27:37,560
What do you mean by that?

452
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:39,100
Anything I want to do?

453
00:27:40,130 --> 00:27:42,770
Well, you can't
just work part-time forever.

454
00:27:43,900 --> 00:27:46,270
I'll give you
all the prize money I won,

455
00:27:46,670 --> 00:27:47,670
so start a business.

456
00:27:48,970 --> 00:27:50,110
Don't be ridiculous.

457
00:27:51,640 --> 00:27:53,440
Why would I start a business
with your money?

458
00:27:54,410 --> 00:27:55,410
No way.

459
00:27:55,580 --> 00:27:56,610
Come on.

460
00:27:58,110 --> 00:28:00,980
I know perfectly well how hard
you worked for that prize money.

461
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:02,950
How could I possibly
take that money?

462
00:28:04,320 --> 00:28:05,560
I appreciate the thought.

463
00:28:06,320 --> 00:28:08,360
So don't say things like that.

464
00:28:09,860 --> 00:28:11,230
Am I not your sister?

465
00:28:14,500 --> 00:28:16,430
I asked if I wasn't your sister.

466
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:21,670
- Ko Eun Seol...
- So just take it.

467
00:28:23,110 --> 00:28:26,580
If you really feel bad about it,
you can pay me back later.

468
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:27,840
Right?

469
00:28:28,710 --> 00:28:29,750
I still can't.

470
00:28:31,710 --> 00:28:33,550
How can I sponge off you too?

471
00:28:35,350 --> 00:28:37,150
No matter how I think about it,
it's just not right.

472
00:28:38,790 --> 00:28:40,160
Do you have that little confidence
in yourself?

473
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:43,430
Just work hard and make it big.

474
00:28:45,660 --> 00:28:46,660
Right?

475
00:28:47,900 --> 00:28:49,070
Answer me.

476
00:28:49,570 --> 00:28:50,570
You'll do that, right?

477
00:28:54,500 --> 00:28:55,670
Are you really saying...

478
00:28:57,040 --> 00:28:58,410
I can spend that money?

479
00:28:59,010 --> 00:29:00,010
Of course.

480
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:02,480
That's the best way to spend it.

481
00:29:07,920 --> 00:29:08,920
Thanks.

482
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:12,560
Thank you so much, little sis.

483
00:29:22,270 --> 00:29:24,470
Director Joo?

484
00:29:25,170 --> 00:29:27,100
- Yes, Chairman Kim.
- Right.

485
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:30,970
Tell the housekeeper to get
dinner ready for a guest tonight.

486
00:29:30,970 --> 00:29:32,440
We're having someone important over.

487
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:33,780
An important guest?

488
00:29:34,010 --> 00:29:35,150
Is it the CEO's guest?

489
00:29:35,380 --> 00:29:36,610
No, it's Eun Seol.

490
00:29:38,350 --> 00:29:39,380
Ko Eun Seol?

491
00:29:40,620 --> 00:29:43,320
I invited her to congratulate her
on her win, among other things.

492
00:29:44,620 --> 00:29:48,690
But I don't think
that's a very good idea, ma'am.

493
00:29:49,490 --> 00:29:50,490
How so?

494
00:29:51,490 --> 00:29:53,560
Well, from Ms. Ko's perspective,

495
00:29:53,760 --> 00:29:56,530
your invitation might feel
overwhelming and uncomfortable.

496
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:57,730
She'll probably feel awkward.

497
00:29:58,970 --> 00:30:02,140
I figured as much,
so I also invited Seok Jin.

498
00:30:02,210 --> 00:30:04,340
I thought it'd be less awkward
if he were here.

499
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:06,740
Chief Cha too?

500
00:30:07,810 --> 00:30:10,150
So tell them
to get everything ready on time.

501
00:30:27,730 --> 00:30:28,730
Hello?

502
00:30:28,830 --> 00:30:31,670
It's me.
Are you coming to my house today?

503
00:30:32,140 --> 00:30:34,340
Yes, the Chairman invited me.

504
00:30:34,800 --> 00:30:36,770
And you're actually coming?

505
00:30:37,610 --> 00:30:38,780
Yes. Why?

506
00:30:39,510 --> 00:30:40,740
Don't come over.

507
00:30:42,250 --> 00:30:43,250
Why not?

508
00:30:43,310 --> 00:30:44,350
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

509
00:30:44,410 --> 00:30:45,880
Your leg hasn't even healed yet.

510
00:30:45,950 --> 00:30:48,020
What if you push yourself
and it gets worse?

511
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:49,750
Just stay home and rest.

512
00:30:50,290 --> 00:30:53,820
Are you telling me not to come
because you're worried about my leg?

513
00:30:54,820 --> 00:30:56,160
Don't worry about that.

514
00:30:56,730 --> 00:30:57,930
I'm taking a taxi.

515
00:30:58,860 --> 00:30:59,960
Hey, Ko Eun Seol.

516
00:31:00,330 --> 00:31:02,370
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

517
00:31:02,470 --> 00:31:03,500
Didn't you hear what I said?

518
00:31:04,070 --> 00:31:05,900
Just don't come to my house.

519
00:31:06,770 --> 00:31:09,640
It'd be rude to the person
who invited me.

520
00:31:10,570 --> 00:31:11,810
I'll see you at your house later.

521
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:14,480
Hey, Ko...

522
00:31:16,510 --> 00:31:17,550
Unbelievable.

523
00:31:21,990 --> 00:31:24,790
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

524
00:31:28,390 --> 00:31:29,590
Excuse me.

525
00:31:32,760 --> 00:31:33,760
I'm sorry about this.

526
00:31:36,700 --> 00:31:38,400
- Hey.
- Seok Jin, where are you?

527
00:31:38,970 --> 00:31:40,070
I'm out of the office. Why?

528
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:41,600
Then when are you coming back?

529
00:31:42,370 --> 00:31:44,940
After I finish up here,
I'm heading straight to your place.

530
00:31:45,480 --> 00:31:46,480
What?

531
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:48,880
Hae Ra,
I can't really talk right now.

532
00:31:48,950 --> 00:31:49,950
I'll see you at your place later.

533
00:31:50,580 --> 00:31:51,580
Sure.

534
00:31:52,950 --> 00:31:53,980
Sorry about that.

535
00:31:54,420 --> 00:31:55,590
Seok Jin!

536
00:31:56,950 --> 00:31:58,020
Seriously.

537
00:31:59,320 --> 00:32:00,860
This is driving me crazy.

538
00:32:15,200 --> 00:32:16,210
Are you okay?

539
00:32:16,940 --> 00:32:17,940
Seok Jin.

540
00:32:18,170 --> 00:32:19,980
- Need a hand?
- I'm okay.

541
00:32:20,380 --> 00:32:21,680
Careful.

542
00:32:22,910 --> 00:32:23,910
Thanks.

543
00:32:28,020 --> 00:32:30,850
You hurt your leg,
so please stay seated.

544
00:32:31,220 --> 00:32:33,490
- But I can't just...
- It's fine,

545
00:32:33,790 --> 00:32:34,790
so please sit.

546
00:32:35,830 --> 00:32:36,830
Sure.

547
00:32:40,860 --> 00:32:41,860
So...

548
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:44,370
Eun Seol, tell us about your family.

549
00:32:44,730 --> 00:32:46,500
Who are you living with now?

550
00:32:48,600 --> 00:32:51,510
My father, my older brother,
and my grandmother.

551
00:32:51,870 --> 00:32:54,280
What about your mom? You had one.

552
00:32:55,410 --> 00:32:56,610
She passed away.

553
00:32:57,410 --> 00:32:58,410
She passed away?

554
00:33:05,020 --> 00:33:08,290
How dare you hit my daughter?
Do you have any idea who you are?

555
00:33:11,160 --> 00:33:12,160
When?

556
00:33:13,300 --> 00:33:14,300
Ten years ago.

557
00:33:14,930 --> 00:33:16,400
Why? How did she die?

558
00:33:51,100 --> 00:33:55,000
(A Trap Called Desire)

559
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:56,640
Aren't you coming back
from the CEO's house?

560
00:33:56,640 --> 00:33:58,270
Did something bad happen there?

561
00:33:58,270 --> 00:33:59,910
From now on,
if you have any concerns,

562
00:33:59,980 --> 00:34:01,040
you can always talk to me.

563
00:34:01,140 --> 00:34:02,610
Be rational.

564
00:34:02,610 --> 00:34:03,910
She's no pushover.

565
00:34:03,910 --> 00:34:05,850
So are you just going to stand by
and do nothing?

566
00:34:05,880 --> 00:34:07,720
Thankfully, we got to know
the real Ko Eun Seol...

567
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:09,290
before it was too late.

568
00:34:09,290 --> 00:34:10,450
Mom, did you say something?

569
00:34:10,550 --> 00:34:12,090
You messed up, didn't you?

570
00:34:12,090 --> 00:34:14,160
Didn't you know when you asked?

571
00:34:14,490 --> 00:34:16,060
What have you been doing
for the past ten years?

572
00:34:16,090 --> 00:34:18,660
What are you hiding?
I said, tell me.

573
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:19,900
Just a moment.

574
00:34:20,500 --> 00:34:22,470
Today's Grand Prize winner,
Ko Eun Seol...

575
00:34:24,130 --> 00:34:26,100
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
